NEX patch for go-gost/x v0.8.1, applied by gost-runtime/build.sh after nex-splice.patch.

Fixes classic-AEAD Shadowsocks UDP (connector "ssu" + dialer "udp"): upstream sent valid
packets but never delivered a single reply, so UDP through an ss egress was one-way.
  1. internal/util/ss/conn.go stored the per-flow session under session.Hash()
     ("aead-<local addr>") and looked it up under SessionHashFromAddrPort(<local addr>)
     ("<local addr>"). The lookup always missed, the first reply returned
     "udp session cannot find" and the relay closed the flow. The session now lives on
     the UDPConn (one conn = one flow); the never-pruned connector-wide map is no longer
     written (it grew by one entry per flow).
  2. Classic AEAD replies are [salt][AEAD(SOCKS addr + payload)]; the address was handed
     to the client as payload. It is now stripped (SS2022 replies are already stripped
     by go-shadowsocks2).
  3. A reply that fails to decrypt or parse is dropped instead of failing the read and
     tearing down the flow.
The salt-filter and SS2022 wire-format fixes are in nex-shadowsocks2.patch (go-gost/go-shadowsocks2).

